WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:07.150
Heaven's Design Team

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.990
This order is for...

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.980
"An animal that tickles 
one's maternal instincts."

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.610
Cheers!

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.690
A-All right, understood!

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.900
So that's the word.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:50.120
Maternal instincts? So, basically an animal 
that makes you want to protect it?

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.880
It sounds fun, but I have 
my hands full right now.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.970
Aw, man. You could go all-out 
making a cute animal!

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.130
But I'm also tied up in other work.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.030
Ah, I see.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.690
Then I'll go ask someone else.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:14.170
I'm in the pursuit of the ultimate 
umami only crustaceans can possess,

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.340
but I'm still not satisfied.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.890
I understand. Good luck.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.440
Everybody's so busy.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.380
Why does it always get busy when
 everybody's already working?

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.800
Is there no one who's free?

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.680
Yes! I'm free. I'll do it!

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.560
Oh... okay.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.910
<i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:40.940
<i>Of course the one who seems least-suited
 to this job is in charge of it now.</i>

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:43.040
<i>I wonder if this'll be okay.</i>

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.300
But that doesn't sound like 
your area of expertise.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.800
Want some help?

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.090
Hm, I think I'd like some advice.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:55.580
All right! Make something super cute, okay?

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.950
Thank you! I'll do my best.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:01.320
<i>At first glance, 
all might seem harmonious,</i>

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.420
<i>but with these two together, 
I get an even worse feeling.</i>

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.590
That's a team that shouldn't 
be allowed to talk about love.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.770
I'm afraid they'll design something 
where the children and parents eat each other.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:18.100
"Tickles the maternal instincts," huh?

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:22.190
What kind of emotion does that evoke?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:24.080
Must be love.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.730
Love, huh?

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.130
Is what you're making right 
now a parent and its child?

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.860
No, that's not it.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:36.770
This is a male imprisoning the female 
with his long legs so she can't get away.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.030
I mean, the ocean is vast, right?

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.970
The chance of meeting a good 
female at the right time is low.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:47.780
That's why he imprisons her in his legs 
so other males can't take her away,

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.300
and waits until it's time for mating.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.610
You're a caged bird.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.080
But did I really capture you?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.440
Perhaps you have captured me.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.350
Uh...

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.480
So love is imprisonment.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.050
Imprison...

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.270
...ment?

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.810
W-Wait, what's this imprisonment 
you're talking about?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:16.520
Pluto-chan, we'd like to help too,
while we're taking a breather.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:21.400
Imprisonment is good, but have you 
considered lovingly carrying the child?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.200
Yeah! That's right.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.030
See, carrying is love!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:30.400
But those twins... One of them 
will be left to die, right?

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.300
Wh-Why would you even think that?!

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.460
I mean, Neptune-san made the panda that way.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.310
They give birth to two and 
keep the bigger one, right?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.940
Two cubs are born, but one's just a backup.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:49.000
W-Well, I only set it up that 
way so they can survive!

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.060
Pandas' bodies having a 
hard time taking in nutrients.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:55.140
It's just for rare emergencies, right?

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.200
Down on Earth, the chances of that 
emergency happening are quite high.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.760
Listen, Pluto-chan...

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:06.610
Bears actually have the ability 
to control when they give birth.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:10.330
After mating with a male, the female 
can put the pregnancy on hold.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.790
<b>A Bear's Life Theater</b>

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.930
I love you!

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.460
I love you!

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.790
Mwah!

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.640
All right, take care of the kids!

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.200
See ya.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.100
If she didn't put it on hold 
and gave birth right away,

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.940
it would get colder and colder...

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.680
There's no food, and it's 
only getting colder.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.410
We can't do this!

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.520
But if she puts the pregnancy 
and birth on hold...

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.580
Heck yeah, it's spring! 
Your mom's gonna do this!

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:38.670
So if conditions aren't difficult for the panda,

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.870
she will properly raise both cubs.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:45.290
But those two cubs are from 
different fathers, right?

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.370
She's seeing two guys?

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:51.870
With that ability, she can see
 different males at different times,

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.480
but give birth all in one go.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:59.280
It may not be the product of devoted 
love between one male and one female,

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:03.450
but this is a strategy devised to 
survive the harsh reality of nature.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:08.270
The hope is that by raising different 
types of cubs, at least one will make it.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:10.000
That was really helpful.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.750
<i>I have a bad feeling about this!</i>

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:15.610
Wait! What part of that 
did you find helpful?

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:17.870
Forget the second half! Hugging!

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.390
Hugging is what love between 
parents and children is!

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:23.130
R-Right! Love between parents and children!

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:27.900
That's right! And the father! 
The father's love is important, too!

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:29.900
The father?

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.910
Yes! The father!

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.760
It's called maternal instinct,

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:37.530
but the love of a parent isn't 
limited to the mother, right?

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:47.300
<b>House 
Sparrow</b>

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.790
There are a lot of animals 
where the father rears the child.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.480
For instance, take a look at this sparrow.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:46.930
That's so cute! They take 
turns feeding the chick.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.110
The father takes part in 
rearing the child, too.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.800
Isn't that wonderful? They're cooperating.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.260
These babies also share 
food with their flock.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.300
Watch this.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.490
Wow, so much food.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:03.810
I have to tell everyone 
about this. Everybody!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.390
Yay, food! Food!

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.820
Oh, you're right.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.010
They're all eating together.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:11.150
See?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.570
Hm...

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.130
Are they really cooperating?

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.480
If they were truly cooperating,

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:23.340
they should be calling their friends even 
if there was just enough food for one bird.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:26.650
Yay, food! But just a little.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.300
It's not calling its friends, huh?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.170
It's actually hogging the food.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.910
Isn't it bad to keep secrets amongst friends?

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:42.660
But it's not like we're making 
these animals to be morally pure.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.310
The jig's up! Oh, well. All that 
matters is my survival!

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:49.920
O-Oh, fine.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.730
The reason they're calling their friends 
is not just for sharing the food.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:57.720
The chance of being attacked 
by a predator is lower

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.000
when they're eating together 
than when they eat alone!

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.870
The "Ate My Money Away" Detective 
sees through all smoke and mirrors!

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.000
You're still doing that bit?

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.930
That was really helpful.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.090
Wait! What part of that 
did you find helpful?

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.930
Forget the second half!

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.750
Remember parental love in the form of 
the father also raising the child!

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.520
Please use that as inspiration!

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:22.980
<b>A Few Hours Later</b>

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.380
All right, here's my presentation.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:31.710
<i>I wonder what she made. 
I'm a little excited, and a little scared...</i>

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.540
Huh, where are Jupiter and Neptune-san?

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:39.270
Jupiter-san was shouting, "It's not the 
big crab's fault that it tastes bad!"

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:42.020
"It's the cooking method's fault!"

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:47.300
Then he went off to Galapagos to put the whole 
crab into a pot without cutting it up.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.560
That guy...

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.810
So he's making pots instead of animals.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:56.820
Neptune-san also went to 
Galapagos to test his bear.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:00.780
But since you're here, 
I'll do my presentation anyway.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:01.590
Yes.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:03.680
First, the visual:

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.330
Round and fluffy.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:07.730
Not good?

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.890
N-No, it was just unexpected!

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.310
Don't mind us. Please, continue.

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:17.830
The father will lovingly carry this.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:21.680
Th-This is unexpected. 
Carrying something fluffy!

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:25.260
Could this lead to the golden 
standard of cuteness?

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:27.830
So that fluffy thing is the child?

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:28.850
No.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:34.140
This white bag is a parasite's egg!

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:40.490
The main body has the ability to burrow into 
the host's body, like the root of a plant.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.670
Then it invades the host's nervous system,

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.680
and makes it think that the 
fluffy thing is its own child.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:51.570
The host will hug this bag to its chest, 
and protect "its child" for the parasite.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:57.870
Oh, and if a male is infested, a hormonal
 imbalance will feminize the host.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.860
<b>I am your mother!</b>

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.360
That's so wonderful.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.360
This is "the animal that tickles 
the maternal instincts"!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:05.860
God has spoken!

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.490
Accepted!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:11.380
<b>Rhizocephala</b>

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:11.380
<b>Main Body</b>

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:11.380
<b>Egg</b>

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:11.380
<b>Package Deal!</b>

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:11.380
<b>Accepted</b>

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:08.960
Yay!

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.390
It already passed?

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:14.000
You haven't even said what it parasitizes.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.570
Oh, that's true.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:19.950
Since you helped me, I'll have 
it infest something you made.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.000
Wait!

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.300
It wouldn't be right for me 
to have the honor alone!

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.730
I-I know!

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:31.400
So you called us all together...

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:35.430
...because more candidates means a lower 
chance that your creation will be picked.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:38.520
Just like when the sparrows 
eat food together.

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.980
I just couldn't stay calm!

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:42.940
This is hard.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.730
I want it to be lovingly held,

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.710
so I'll go for the crab, since it
 has so many arms to hug with!

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.930
Thank you!

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.440
I'm safe!

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.700
Congratulations, Jupiter-kun.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:59.930
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.970
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.810
So the crab thinks this 
fluffy thing on its abdomen

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:06.170
is its own egg sac, and it's 
guarding it vigilantly.

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:09.170
But those are really the eggs of the 
Rhizocephala parasite.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:12.190
I wonder how the crab feels about that.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:16.210
Not sure, but infested crabs have long lives.

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:20.430
That's because they don't use energy for 
reproduction and take care of themselves instead.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:22.930
So it's not all that bad, then.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:26.230
What are Rhizocephala anyway? Insects?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:28.440
No, they're crustaceans.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:31.460
Crustaceans? So, relatives of the crab?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.950
Is a crab hitching a ride on a crab, then?

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:38.190
That means the eggs might be tasty.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.340
<b>Tasting. . .</b>

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.700
Tastes a bit like urchin. I might like this.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:49.630
I like Rhizocephala, too. 
We're the same, Jupiter-san.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:00.400
<b>WHICH ONE WILL BE ACCEPTED?</b>

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:00.400
<b>The</b>

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:59.880
<i>Which One Will Be Accepted? The Show!</i>

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.500
Welcome, everyone!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.100
It's time for <i>Which One 
Will Be Accepted? The Show!</i>

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:12.150
Today's request is for "a bird 
that lives on an island of ice"!

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:17.370
Here, our Heaven's Design Team is 
about to have a presentation battle!

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:22.280
Our commentators will be Venus-san, with 
her motto, "To design is to create beauty..."

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:22.050
<b>Venus</b>

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.590
<b>Commentators</b>

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.580
And Saturn-san, who says, 
"Horses are the best!"

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.590
<b>Saturn</b>

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:27.690
Can I have a word from 
you two about today's battle?

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:31.350
The best way to counteract 
the cold is to put on fat.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:35.350
I believe the contestants will 
make fat, flightless birds.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.700
If it's an island of ice, 
there won't be many enemies,

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:39.670
so being flightless should be fine.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:41.870
I see! That's an excellent prediction!

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:43.490
All right then, contestants,

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.490
please do your best 
in the presentation battle!

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:50.560
Um, I'm looking forward to 
making a cute roundie.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:50.700
<b>Neptune</b>

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:55.370
<b>Jupiter</b>

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:55.370
I will do everything I can to keep 
it from being round and cute.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.500
And the battle is on!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.500
<b>JUPITER</b>

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.500
<b>NEPTUNE</b>

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:04.880
<b>Question</b>

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:04.880
<b>What's the ideal amphibious body
 for living on an island of ice!?</b>

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.150
Question 1!

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:04.890
What's the ideal amphibious body 
for living on an island of ice?

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.790
I'm surprised Shimoda-kun's so enthusiastic.

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:10.880
Speaking of, apparently he knows 
quite a bit about rap, too.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.300
This is mine.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.260
Then this is mine.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:21.390
Oh, they both look the 
same... Wait a minute.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.400
Those legs are so long!

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:29.400
Their coloring is the same, 
but now we have both leg extremes!

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.250
What do you say, Venus-san?

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:33.910
As expected, both of them are good.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.170
Did you hear this? High praise!

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:40.330
For the fish, this coloring 
is the hardest to spot.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.780
Since it's dark in the deep, 
black is hard to see.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.920
Since the surface is blinding, 
white's also hard to see.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:49.350
This reminds me of Pluto-kun's squid.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.830
Indeed, this is like the 
smokescreen of light!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.990
Then let's switch over to 
Mars-san and get her judgment.

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.430
Mars-san, are you ready?

00:13:57.610 --> 00:13:58.910
Yes, I'm here.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.460
Hello, I'm currently on Galapagos.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:05.160
I've covered the island with ice, 
so we'll be testing the birds here.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.080
Should I send you a visual?

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.340
All right, it looks like the battle 
will take place there!

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:14.050
Who will the goddess of 
victory favor this time?!

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:17.340
<i>Uh, what's going on, here?</i>

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.280
The presentation right before this 
one left a bit of bad taste in my mouth.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:24.950
That's why Shimoda-kun suggested 
a light-hearted competition.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:27.960
From time to time, something like this is fine.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.320
<i>Uh... thank you for the explanation.</i>

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:34.920
<i>Well, whatever. I'll have the 
two birds go to the ocean now.</i>

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:38.720
<i>It'll be a race to see who
 can catch a fish faster!</i>

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:41.330
Ready, set, go!

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:44.860
<i>You got this!</i>

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:45.960
<i>Nice!</i>

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:57.390
All right, that's elegant!

00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:59.500
Now, a question for the contestants.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:02.010
How does your bird swim?

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.130
<b>Light! Weak!</b>

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:04.890
Its flaps its arms to propel itself forward.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.220
<b>Heavy! Robust!</b>

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:08.270
Since it doesn't fly, I was able to 
make its bones thick and sturdy.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:11.770
Did you forget how much trouble I went 
through to make the birdies light?!

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.450
Mine also kicks its legs!

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:16.530
Wow, that looks fast!

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.630
And they're already back!

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.760
Were they able to catch a fish?

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.510
Who reigned supreme?!

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:27.200
The difference is clear as day!

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.900
Team Neptune was able to secure a fish.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:35.020
<i>Looks like the one with the shorter 
legs is a better swimmer.</i>

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.910
I thought the leg kick would 
make for a faster swimmer.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:43.190
<i>Actually, no. Kicking your legs 
increases your water resistance,</i>

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.480
<i>so that's more of a hindrance.</i>

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:49.690
Down! Our usual trope is 
back with a vengeance!

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:52.420
Mars-san, what's the cause here?

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:54.510
Hypothermia.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:58.660
The cold! Downed by the cold!

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.730
That's fatal in the coldest of seas!

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:06.190
Looks like the one with the long 
legs got cold in the ocean.

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:11.070
With legs that long, it has 
a lot of exposed surface area.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:17.400
The rounder an animal's body is, 
the smaller the area exposed to the elements.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.370
You know how wolves do that, too?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.770
Now that you mention it...

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.290
Hold up!

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:26.970
If that's true, the short-legged one shouldn't
 be able to stand on the ice for so long!

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:30.340
I had a reason for making the legs long.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:32.420
<b>Chilled 
by the ice</b>

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:34.420
With the long legs, we can entwine 
cold veins with warm arteries,

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:34.510
<b>Entwined
 blood vessels</b>

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:37.220
<b>Doesn't get cold</b>

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:36.360
thereby equalizing the temperature.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:50.860
<b>Chilled 
by the ice</b>

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:50.860
<b>Body gets cold</b>

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:38.700
With short legs,

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:41.220
there's no room for
 the temperatures to equalize.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:44.530
The cold blood goes straight into the body.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:47.470
Oh, that sounds unpleasantly chilly!

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:50.860
So there was a reason for those long legs.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.290
But this one doesn't look like it'll collapse.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:55.410
Is its core not cold?

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:56.860
Why not?!

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:00.670
Actually, that one has long legs, too.

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:03.480
They're squatting inside their bodies.

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:07.620
It's like doing a Slav squat, 
then pulling your jacket over your knees.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.500
To see Neptune-kun squat like that...

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.880
That's a rare sight.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:16.650
Imagine that! Neptune-san also made 
the legs long to thwart the cold!

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:21.100
Neptune-san pulls ahead 
with the first point!

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.650
Ah, that's what that is for.

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:25.710
I won't lose the next round!

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.390
Then let's get to the next question!

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.900
<b>Question</b>

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.900
<b>How do you ensure that the fish 
don't get away?</b>

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.440
How do you ensure that the fish don't get away?

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:37.120
I made its beak big and jagged.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:40.670
That's so it can have a good grip 
on the fish while it swims.

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:41.700
I see!

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:46.180
On the other hand, Jupiter-san's 
bird doesn't look visibly changed.

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.450
Did that surprise you?

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:52.920
Hey! Can you not break the bounds 
of the bird category?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.930
Mars-kun, what's your verdict here?

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:58.280
<i>Both of them have issues.</i>

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:01.670
<i>A bigger beak means that 
more heat escapes through it,</i>

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:02.730
<i>so it might get cold.</i>

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:08.410
<i>The problem with Jupiter-san's idea is that 
opening the mouth so wide lets heat escape, too.</i>

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:11.080
<i>Barbs on the tongue are a good idea, though,</i>

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:13.570
<i>They make it harder 
for fish to get away.</i>

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.730
Jupiter-san's idea is accepted!

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:16.940
Yay!

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.920
All right, then let's make the tongue barbed.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.940
Onto the next question, then!

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:26.830
<b>Question</b>

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:26.830
<b>Can it survive by drinking sea water?</b>

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:26.440
Can it survive by drinking sea water?!

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:33.420
Ven-chan, aren't there already a few 
coastal animals that have this ability?

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.550
There are quite a few animals

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:39.480
that filter out salt from the water 
and eject it through some body fluid.

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:41.500
Then he'll dispose of it through tears.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:42.900
No, through snot!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.600
<b>Sea Gull Style</b>

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.600
<b>Sea Turtle Style</b>

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:49.500
I always felt bad for sea turtles because 
they're crying while laying their eggs.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.720
They're just disposing of 
salt through their eyes.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.860
I never knew.

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:58.500
Then over to you, Mars-san!

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:02.380
<i>Right, tears versus snot. Let's take a look.</i>

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:09.730
Oh, this one goes to snot.

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:11.730
Snot can be shaken off,

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:15.030
but the tears leave the 
face encrusted with salt.

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:20.960
That means Jupiter-san gets yet 
another point and is in the lead!

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:27.230
The sea turtle is almost always in 
the water, so the tears don't dry.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.070
Right.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.560
<b>Question</b>

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.560
<b>The chick design!</b>

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.570
Now, the next question is about the chick design!

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:33.710
The chick needs to be cute!

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:35.670
The chick needs to be safe.

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:39.750
<i>The thorns will keep both 
friend and foe away!</i>

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.310
<i>Since that prevents huddling 
to stay warm, that's rejected!</i>

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.420
Neptune-san's fluffy one wins!

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:50.080
<b>Question</b>

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:50.080
<b>What's its secret for staying underwater
for a long time?</b>

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:49.310
Next question: What's its secret for 
staying underwater for a long time?

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:50.080
What will they do?!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.250
Breathe in a lot of air?

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.170
No, that'll make it float...

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:58.190
Let's make it a poikilotherm, 
then lower the temperature of organs

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.580
not used underwater, to the point
 where it's half-dead.

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:02.110
<i>That's good!</i>

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:04.970
<i>That'll lower its oxygen consumption.</i>

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:08.070
Being half-dead while 
swimming sure is novel.

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:11.230
That may be too novel to still be a bird.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.160
The point goes to Jupiter-san!

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.980
<b>Question</b>

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.980
<b>How will the children recognize
 their parents</b>

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:16.980
Next up: How will the children 
recognize their parents?

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:20.360
The parent will talk to it before it hatches, 
letting the child learn its voice.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:19.110
<b>I'm your dad</b>

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:20.360
<b>Dad</b>

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.810
Each face will have a different pattern.

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:24.600
<i>You can't see a pattern in a snow storm.</i>

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:25.240
<i>Rejected.</i>

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.740
That's a point for Neptune-san!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.830
Neither of them are yielding, 
and we go into the final round with a tie!

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.900
The battle for the bird that lives on 
an icy island has become really heated!

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.620
Let's hear how our two 
contestants are feeling!

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:40.590
How is it going, Neptune-san?

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:44.380
Um, this is harder than I thought.
 I'll do my best.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:46.640
Jupiter-san, how about you?

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:50.100
A lot more passed than I expected.

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:53.280
I just did the opposite 
of Neptune-san's ideas.

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:57.040
Oh! That's brutally honest!

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:00.880
Now, let us move on to the final question!

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:58.270
<b>What if there's no food while raising the child</b>

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:03.150
<b>Question</b>

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:03.150
What if there's no food while raising the child?

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:07.120
That's a key factor for surviving 
in extreme cold.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.910
What are your answers?!

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:10.980
The parents will fast!

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:12.150
Poor things!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:13.900
The chicks will fast!

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:15.770
Poor things!

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:19.180
Mars-san, what is your judgment here?

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:21.400
That's really hard to say.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:25.040
Since they're flightless, 
they can pack on body fat,

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:27.070
so their bodies are suited to fasting.

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:28.880
But which to pick?

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:29.800
Who...

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:32.080
Who will be the winner?!

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:38.830
Both are accepted!

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:41.070
<b>King Penguin {left}</b>

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:41.070
<b>Emperor Penguin</b>

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:41.070
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:41.070
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.400
God has spoken!

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:44.080
<i>Literally the Word of God!</i>

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.570
Congratulations, Neptune-san, Jupiter-san!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:54.510
Since both were accepted by God,

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:57.840
you're apparently free to add a 
quality of your own choosing.

00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:00.940
Then I'll make an alternate 
design for the chick.

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:03.190
That chick is accepted, too!

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:04.340
<b>Accepted</b>

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.340
<b>Emperor Penguin
 Chick</b>

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.510
I'll, hmm... get rid of the round 
pupils and make them square.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:14.980
<b>Accepted</b>

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:12.590
That's kind of scary!

00:22:12.590 --> 00:22:14.340
I'm so happy.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:46.480
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
